{
 "name": "poly_merge_boundary_divergence",
 "face_ring_start": "ignored",
 "face_ring_start_note": "This case's gap is EMPTY and was closed by writing one block into both `reference` and `vibe3d_current` -- they are byte-identical. Under the rotation-tolerant reading that is exact and harmless. Under a strict one it is not: measured 2026-08-18, our LIVE merge product begins its ring at a different corner from the block in both slots, so the `vibe3d_current` tuples here are the reference's numbers and not a record of ours. Declaring \"compared\" would therefore assert the reference's ring start as if we reproduced it, and we do not. Re-measuring OUR side is what this needs -- see doc/tasks/backlog/1311-ring-start-laws-to-capture.md.",
 "description": "Merging a polygon selection into one face: which boundary the merge walks. Two measured cells, both CLOSED by task 1220; the declared gap is empty in the vertex AND the face channel and the runner recomputes both live, so any drift on either side reddens this suite. (a) An ANNULUS -- a 3x3 grid of quads with the centre face missing, all 8 faces selected. The reference emits one face whose ring has 18 corners: the walk enters the hole along the edge (2,0,2)-(2,0,3), goes round the hole and leaves along that same edge, so both of those vertices stand in the ring twice; it keeps all 16 vertices and 17 edges. As measured we emitted the 12-corner OUTER boundary only -- the hole paved over and the 4 vertices that bounded it deleted, 12 vertices and 12 edges. `removeEdgesByMask` now keeps walking after the first closed loop and bridges the leftover rims into it along one interior edge, so we return the same 18-corner keyhole. (b) Two quads that share an edge but are wound OPPOSITELY. The reference merges them into one hexagon (6 vertices, 6 edges, 1 face). As measured we left both quads standing, shared edge and all (2 faces, 7 edges) -- the vertex set is identical on both sides, so this cell is invisible to any check that compares vertices alone. The same kernel now orients the whole component from its first face before the walk, and the two half-edges of the shared edge cancel.",
 "source": "Reference side: headless command-port capture of the merge command on the two bases below (dirty-geometry sweep, task 1123, cases merge_all_grid_hole / merge_all_wind_flip). vibe3d side: live drive of this build through the steps stored in each case.",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
